{
 "nodes": [
  {
   "id": "cap-btitle",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -1900,
   "y": -600,
   "width": 1500,
   "height": 200,
   "text": "# GLM-5.3-Flash — one decoder layer  \nmHC reads the 4 residual lanes → RMSNorm → **token mixer** → mHC writes back → mHC reads → RMSNorm → **MoE** → mHC writes back. Left four columns = the **MLA + DSA** mixer (11 layers: L3, L7, … L43); right column = the **KDA** mixer (34 layers). Grey bars = tensors (0.05 px/channel, long ones clipped); boxes = operations with their weights per layer."
  },
  {
   "id": "cap-bnote",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -300,
   "y": -600,
   "width": 1500,
   "height": 200,
   "text": "**Layer variants.** L0–2 use a dense SwiGLU FFN 4096→12288→4096 (151.0M) instead of the MoE. Mixer weights per layer: KDA **137.7M**, MLA + indexer **124.9M**. The two mHC mixers are 393K each. Every DSA layer has its own indexer (indexer_types all \"full\"). Checkpoint stores q/k/v short convs and each expert as separate tensors; transformers fuses them on load."
  },
  {
   "id": "bx1",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -240,
   "y": -330,
   "width": 480,
   "height": 9,
   "text": "",
   "color": "#64748b"
  },
  {
   "id": "note-lbl2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 260,
   "y": -342,
   "width": 300,
   "height": 34,
   "text": "`X [T, 4, 4096] lanes from previous layer` — bar clipped (real 819px)"
  },
  {
   "id": "bhc13",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -150,
   "y": -281,
   "width": 300,
   "height": 80,
   "text": "**mHC read** (attn_hc): RMSNorm(flatten 16384) → 24 weights; x = Σ pre·X  \n393K",
   "color": "#e879f9"
  },
