  },
  {
   "id": "note-kv",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1300,
   "y": -600,
   "width": 420,
   "height": 200,
   "text": "Why MLA: the cache keeps one 512-value latent per token instead of 64 heads × (256+256) keys and values (32,768 numbers); kv_b_proj re-expands it. The indexer also caches 257 values / token. KDA instead keeps a fixed 64×128×128 state."
  },
  {
   "id": "note-hc",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -1900,
   "y": 1131,
   "width": 900,
   "height": 130,
   "text": "**mHC** (4 lanes): per token, a 16384→24 projection gives pre [4] (how to read the lanes), post [4] (how to write the output back) and comb [4×4] (how lanes mix), comb made doubly stochastic by 20 Sinkhorn steps so the stream norm cannot blow up."
  }
 ],
